From: mix2-port <mix2@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] drm/panel: add JDI NT35596S panel of the Xiaomi Mi MIX 2

Started from linux-mdss-dsi-panel-driver-generator output for the panel
node (qcom,mdss_dsi_jdi_fhd_nt35596s_video) of the stock Xiaomi device tree,
then fixed up on the device:

- timings and DSI mode as read back from the DSI controller the bootloader
  programs: non-burst with sync events, no HSE (the stock DT says burst+HSE,
  which upsets the in-cell touch)
- the stock on-command (long_init, default) and the XBL panel XML sequence;
  the generator had turned the 1-byte 0x51 writes into 2-byte brightness
- handover (default): keep the panel the bootloader brought up at boot
- never send display off / sleep in: this panel then stops answering on the
  link for good. The supplies stay on and every later prepare resets and
  initialises it again (the backlight is switched off meanwhile)
---
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/panel/Kconfig	2026-10-25 17:08:39.643437829 +0800
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/panel/Kconfig	2026-10-25 17:08:39.643560686 +0800
@@ -339,6 +339,16 @@
 	  24 bit per pixel.
 
 
+config DRM_PANEL_JDI_NT35596S
+	tristate "JDI NT35596S FHD+ video mode panel (Xiaomi Mi MIX 2)"
+	depends on OF
+	depends on DRM_MIPI_DSI
+	depends on BACKLIGHT_CLASS_DEVICE
+	help
+	  Say Y here if you want to enable support for the JDI 1080x2160
+	  video mode DSI panel with the Novatek NT35596S driver IC found in
+	  the Xiaomi Mi MIX 2 (chiron).
+
 config DRM_PANEL_JDI_R63452
 	tristate "JDI R63452 Full HD DSI panel"
 	depends on OF
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/panel/Makefile	2026-10-25 17:08:39.643484252 +0800
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/panel/Makefile	2026-10-25 17:08:39.643681583 +0800
@@ -34,6 +34,7 @@
 obj-$(CONFIG_DRM_PANEL_JADARD_JD9365DA_H3) += panel-jadard-jd9365da-h3.o
 obj-$(CONFIG_DRM_PANEL_JDI_LT070ME05000) += panel-jdi-lt070me05000.o
 obj-$(CONFIG_DRM_PANEL_JDI_LPM102A188A) += panel-jdi-lpm102a188a.o
+obj-$(CONFIG_DRM_PANEL_JDI_NT35596S) += panel-jdi-nt35596s.o
 obj-$(CONFIG_DRM_PANEL_JDI_R63452) += panel-jdi-fhd-r63452.o
 obj-$(CONFIG_DRM_PANEL_KHADAS_TS050) += panel-khadas-ts050.o
 obj-$(CONFIG_DRM_PANEL_KINGDISPLAY_KD097D04) += panel-kingdisplay-kd097d04.o
